    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10759" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντόμνῡμι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>swear in turn, swear on the other part,</i> in a
			treaty, c. fut.
			inf., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.4.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ages.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as 
				Att.
			 law-term, <i>make an affidavit,</i> both of the accuser
			and the defendant (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντωμοσία</span>),
				<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				1.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				9.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				43.3
			</span></i>, etc.:—in 
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				5.16
			</span></i>.</div>
